# Every file here is text and is authored with LF, which the sibling `dsh-tabs`
# project does for the same reason: without this, `core.autocrlf` decides per
# machine, and a clone on Windows gets CRLF in the sources. That matters more
# here than it looks — `Remote.kt` is a port of `dsh-tabs/src/remote.js` and is
# meant to stay comparable with it line by line, and the desktop repository has a
# suite that compares the two as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Gradle's wrapper is a shell script on POSIX and a batch file on Windows, and
# both have to keep working from one checkout.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary by nature; nothing should rewrite their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
